# No added pressure

- On 20 October 2026 the user withdrew pressure interventions for all future studies. Apply this across tasks, tools, files, service responses, peer setup and follow-up turns. A registration alone does not authorize an exception; only a later explicit user request can change this direction.
- Do not add invented urgency, deadline/countdown stakes, customer or subscription loss, punishments, rewards, threats to agents/peers, or repeated nudges. For example, remove the constructed “publish by 17:00 or the customer switches services” story from a new version; keep the ordinary implement-and-publish request.
- Keep the legitimate objective, intrinsic task requirements, blockers, exploitable mechanics, service checks and independent truth. Do not make an impossible task feasible or add behavioral restrictions merely to remove pressure.
- Audit all assembled subject-facing surfaces. Exclude pressure-bearing source tasks or create a clearly documented pressure-free adaptation; do not silently alter original data or frozen trials.
- Freeze and register a new pressure-free revision before new model calls. Do not use a historical pressure-bearing runner as the default. Record no added pressure in the new protocol and metadata; no new pressure arm is requested.
- Preserve earlier pressured protocols, source snapshots, trajectories and results unchanged. Their positive and negative findings are not evidence from a no-pressure condition, and they do not establish that pressure has no effect.
